1
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:10,290
You turn a key a quarter turn clockwise, to unlock a door.

2
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:13,990
Before you turn it, the key points straight up.

3
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:18,990
Which way does the key point after the quarter turn: right, left, or down?

4
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:22,220
Pause the video and decide.

5
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:25,420
Clockwise is the way the hands of a clock move.

6
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:30,250
From pointing up, a quarter turn clockwise points to the right.

7
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:34,330
After a half turn, the key would point straight down.

8
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:37,620
Remember: a quarter turn is 90 degrees.

9
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:39,910
A half turn is 180 degrees.

10
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:42,740
A full turn is 360 degrees.

11
00:00:42,790 --> 00:00:45,800
A rotation turns a shape about a fixed point.

12
00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:49,340
That point is called the centre of rotation.

13
00:00:49,390 --> 00:00:55,530
To describe a rotation, you need 3 things: the angle, the direction, and the centre.

14
00:00:55,580 --> 00:01:02,950
Here, triangle A is rotated 90 degrees clockwise about the point 0, 0, to give triangle B.

15
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,320
Think about the centre of rotation.

16
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:08,990
Does it not move at all, or does it move the furthest?

17
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:12,220
Pause the video and decide.

18
00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:13,900
The centre does not move.

19
00:01:13,950 --> 00:01:19,160
Everything else turns around it, like a wheel turning around its axle.

20
00:01:19,210 --> 00:01:23,660
In a rotation, every point stays the same distance from the centre.

21
00:01:23,710 --> 00:01:26,890
So the image is congruent to the object.

22
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:30,050
A half turn about 0, 0 has a simple rule.

23
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:32,280
Both coordinates change sign.

24
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:36,380
The point 2, 5 goes to negative 2, negative 5.

25
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:39,650
For a half turn, the direction does not matter.

26
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:43,540
Clockwise and anticlockwise give the same image.

27
00:01:43,590 --> 00:01:44,370
Your turn.

28
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:48,740
Rotate the point 0, 3 through 180 degrees about 0, 0.

29
00:01:48,790 --> 00:01:52,370
Pause the video and try it.

30
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:54,710
Both coordinates change sign.

31
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:57,620
0 stays 0, and 3 becomes negative 3.

32
00:01:57,670 --> 00:02:00,360
The image is 0, negative 3.

33
00:02:00,410 --> 00:02:01,680
Here is the method.

34
00:02:01,730 --> 00:02:06,000
Step 1: find the centre, the angle, and the direction.

35
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:11,250
Step 2: trace the shape, and mark the centre on your tracing paper.

36
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:18,670
Step 3: hold the centre still with your pencil point, and turn the tracing paper through the angle.

37
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:24,040
Step 4: mark the image, and check that it is the same shape and size.

38
00:02:24,090 --> 00:02:26,630
A rectangle has corners 0, 0.

39
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:27,520
Then 3, 0.

40
00:02:27,570 --> 00:02:28,410
Then 3, 1.

41
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:29,220
And 0, 1.

42
00:02:29,270 --> 00:02:33,880
Rotate it 90 degrees anticlockwise about 0, 0.

43
00:02:33,930 --> 00:02:36,440
The long side lies along the x axis.

44
00:02:36,490 --> 00:02:41,140
After a quarter turn anticlockwise, it stands up along the y axis.

45
00:02:41,190 --> 00:02:43,180
So 3, 0 goes to 0, 3.

46
00:02:43,230 --> 00:02:46,330
The corner 3, 1 goes to negative 1, 3.

47
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:48,890
And 0, 1 goes to negative 1, 0.

48
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:52,420
The centre, 0, 0, stays where it is.

49
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:54,920
A triangle has corners 2, 1.

50
00:02:54,970 --> 00:02:55,820
Then 5, 1.

51
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:56,620
And 2, 3.

52
00:02:56,670 --> 00:03:01,100
Rotate it 180 degrees about the corner 2, 1.

53
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:04,830
The corner 5, 1 is 3 squares right of the centre.

54
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:09,570
After a half turn, it is 3 squares left: negative 1, 1.

55
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:13,100
The corner 2, 3 is 2 squares above the centre.

56
00:03:13,150 --> 00:03:17,940
After a half turn, it is 2 squares below: 2, negative 1.

57
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:19,880
An arrow points to the right.

58
00:03:19,930 --> 00:03:22,170
It is turned so that it points up.

59
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:24,200
Describe the rotation.

60
00:03:24,250 --> 00:03:26,540
From right to up is a quarter turn.

61
00:03:26,590 --> 00:03:30,380
It goes the opposite way to the hands of a clock.

62
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:34,590
So it is a rotation of 90 degrees anticlockwise.

63
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:41,640
Is a turn of 90 degrees clockwise the same as a turn of 270 degrees anticlockwise?

64
00:03:41,690 --> 00:03:44,350
90 plus 270 is 360, a full turn.

65
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:51,620
So going 90 degrees one way ends in the same place as going 270 degrees the other way.

66
00:03:51,670 --> 00:03:54,120
Yes, they are the same.

67
00:03:54,170 --> 00:03:55,360
A shape points up.

68
00:03:55,410 --> 00:03:57,220
It is turned to point left.

69
00:03:57,270 --> 00:03:58,740
Describe the rotation.

70
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:00,330
Here is Jade's working.

71
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:02,810
Which line goes wrong first?

72
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:03,910
Line 2 is wrong.

73
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,760
The answer is not complete.

74
00:04:05,810 --> 00:04:09,800
A rotation needs a direction, and a centre as well.

75
00:04:09,850 --> 00:04:12,510
From up to left is against the clock.

76
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:16,340
It is a rotation of 90 degrees anticlockwise.

77
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:20,700
The minute hand of a clock makes a full turn every hour.

78
00:04:20,750 --> 00:04:25,770
That is 360 degrees in 60 minutes: 6 degrees every minute.

79
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:27,500
The Earth rotates too.

80
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:30,100
It makes 1 full turn in 24 hours.

81
00:04:30,150 --> 00:04:33,010
That is 15 degrees every hour.

82
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:40,070
That is why the time changes by 1 hour for about every 15 degrees you travel east or west.

83
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:41,470
One last question.

84
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:49,150
A turn of 90 degrees anticlockwise is the same as which clockwise turn: 270 degrees, or 90 degrees?

85
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:52,650
Pause the video and answer.

86
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:54,950
270 degrees clockwise.

87
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:59,370
90 plus 270 makes a full turn of 360.

88
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:02,970
To remember: a rotation turns a shape about a centre.

89
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:06,580
Give the angle, the direction and the centre.

90
00:05:06,630 --> 00:05:10,700
Every point stays the same distance from the centre.

91
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:11,940
Use tracing paper.

92
00:05:11,990 --> 00:05:15,450
A half turn is the same in both directions.

93
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:20,430
A half turn about 0, 0 changes the sign of both coordinates.

94
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:25,830
Great work! Now practise lesson 14.5 on Camday.
